# npm >= 10 warns "Use --omit=dev instead" whenever NODE_ENV=production turns on
# the legacy `production` config. Setting omit explicitly (the recommended
# modern config) silences that warning while keeping the same install behavior:
# production installs skip devDependencies. Railway's build command overrides
# this with `npm install --include=dev` so the build still gets dev tooling.
# omit=dev